// ROUND 48 -- throttles for the aura-tick lightning strike (see
// _updatePassiveEffects). At most this many bolts land per aura tick, and no
// single monster is struck more often than the cooldown, so a pack standing
// in a wide aura reads as a storm rolling through it rather than as one
// opaque sheet of overlapping sprites. The cooldown sits just under the
// 1.2s aura tickInterval so a lone monster still gets a bolt every tick.
const AURA_BOLTS_PER_TICK = 4;

// ROUND 117 -- how many composed-cast particle emitters may run at once. The
// worst case is not a player ultimate, it is a damage aura ticking into a pack:
// twelve monsters in radius, one cast each, on a 0.5s interval. Twelve is the
// ceiling at which that still holds 60fps on the two-core box the suites run
// on; past it the emitter is simply skipped and the sprite layers still play,
// so the cast never disappears -- it just stops throwing sparks.
const FX_EMITTER_CAP = 12;

// ROUND 60 -- the title backdrop. Eighteen plates of the real world, captured
// from the running game across all four regions, one every twenty seconds as
// the user asked. Shuffled per visit so the same region does not open the game
// every single time.
