// ROUND 95 -- the longest road a shipment contract will post. 260 tiles is
// about ninety seconds beside the cart at CART_SPEED; beyond that the contract
// stops being a journey and becomes a commute. See the note in the escort
// branch of `_makeOffer`.
//
// ROUND 144 -- A QUARTER OF A REGION, and this is a correction to the reason
// as much as to the number.
//
// The world doubled this round, which put twice the ground between every two
// towns -- and the nearest pair of quest boards in any region went from 222
// tiles apart to 444, past a cap of 260. So the escort contract stopped being
// postable ANYWHERE, silently: `test_round64`'s "a board is no longer only
// 'kill this monster'" caught it as 13 kinds on the boards against 14
// declared, which is the check doing precisely its job.
//
// The fix is not to raise the number, it is to notice what the number was
// approximating. "Ninety seconds beside the cart" was never the point; the
// point was ONE TOWN OVER rather than across the country, and 260 was what
// that measured in a 1024-tile region. A quarter of a region still measures
// it, and will still measure it if the world moves again. It is a longer walk
// now, because the towns are farther apart now, which is what was asked for.
//
// ROUND 175 -- AND IT IS A WALK, SO MEASURE IT IN MINUTES.
//
// A quarter of a region did not survive the map either. Measured at every
// board in the game, the nearest other settlement is:
