//   nek 337-465 tiles | ontaria 440-491 | elehyd 416-672 | bratugal 529-673
//   sirukh 781-831    | cinder 544-601  | ixcuatl 267-718
//
// against a cap of 532. So FOUR of the seven regions cannot post an escort at
// any seed, and three of those four -- sirukh, cinder, ixcuatl -- shipped
// after round 168 measured this and have never been measured at all. Round
// 168 wrote Bratugal's silence into `surgeChains.js` as a fact about the map;
// it is a fact about this line.
//
// A region's own towns are as far apart as they are, and the NEAREST OTHER
// ONE is "one town over" by definition -- there is no closer place to send a
// cart. Tying the cap to the region's size says otherwise in four regions,
// and the third time a number has to be re-derived because the map moved is
// the point at which the number was measuring the wrong thing.
//
// What round 95 was actually protecting is stated in its own first sentence:
// "about ninety seconds beside the cart at CART_SPEED". The concern is how
// long the player holds a direction. So that is the unit: four minutes at the
// cart's own speed, which covers the longest first-choice road in the game
// (Dunmouth to Salt Gate, 831 tiles, 253 seconds) and still refuses the
// cross-country hauls, every one of which is over a thousand tiles.
//
// It moves with the CART, which is the thing it is about, and will not need
// re-deriving the next time the world grows.
const CART_SPEED_UNITS = 105;             // and `CART_SPEED` returns this one
// ROUND 190 -- 245, not 240. Once the boards moved to their Society halls,
