//
//    r145:   960 / 1.25 = 768      600 / 1.25 = 480
//    r146:  1920 / 2.5  = 768     1200 / 2.5  = 480
//
// Identical. Twice the pixels across the same ground, which is the whole round.
// Measured in the running game rather than argued from this comment -- see
// test_round146_canvas.cjs, which asserts the 768 x 480 rather than the 2.5.
//
// Round 46's reasoning below is untouched: 1.25 was the midpoint between the
